WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:03.920
- [Mark Trent] Nothing has
been so true in my career

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.087
as shoot what I know, and
what I know is West Virginia.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.968
There's something about
this state and the people

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:18.168
that live here, and the
generosity that happens.

00:00:18.168 --> 00:00:19.726
People aren't afraid to
roll up their sleeves

00:00:19.726 --> 00:00:21.229
and help their neighbors,
people aren't afraid

00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:23.646
to pick you up when you fall.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.819
My name is Mark Trent.

00:00:34.819 --> 00:00:37.259
I don't wanna say follow my
dreams, because that's...

00:00:37.259 --> 00:00:38.509
We'll get this.

00:00:40.148 --> 00:00:43.981
I used to work in New
York making commercials.

00:00:45.269 --> 00:00:48.297
I was traveling all the
time, I was living the dream,

00:00:48.297 --> 00:00:52.528
I guess, but I was working
on some personal work

00:00:52.528 --> 00:00:55.608
in my home state of West
Virginia that involves

00:00:55.608 --> 00:00:58.097
prescription drug abuse in the region.

00:00:58.097 --> 00:01:00.600
That's one of the reasons
why I bought my Subaru,

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.389
I had to get down to West Virginia more,

00:01:02.389 --> 00:01:03.777
that was my goal.

00:01:03.777 --> 00:01:05.829
There came a point where I had to choose

00:01:05.829 --> 00:01:09.128
between my life in New
York and my life here,

00:01:09.128 --> 00:01:11.211
and I chose my life here.

00:01:13.928 --> 00:01:16.896
So when I moved back to
West Virginia, I came here

00:01:16.896 --> 00:01:21.374
to kind of focus on the projects
that I was passionate about

00:01:21.374 --> 00:01:25.541
and when the flood happened,
everything was put on hold.

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:30.760
It was the worst flood
in West Virginia history,

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:35.309
in a sense, and it happened
in a matter of minutes.

00:01:35.309 --> 00:01:37.058
I mean, people didn't
notice until it was too late

00:01:37.058 --> 00:01:40.141
and they were trapped in their homes.

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:44.909
After the storm, people from everywhere,

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:47.968
all over the country came to help.

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:50.029
That was one of the
most surprising things,

00:01:50.029 --> 00:01:52.949
the way people just banded together.

00:01:52.949 --> 00:01:56.778
I'd lived in New York for so
many years, I'd lost my sense

00:01:56.778 --> 00:01:59.069
of community, and then just coming
home and seeing that love

00:01:59.069 --> 00:02:03.381
and that support, no one that
needed anything went without

00:02:03.381 --> 00:02:04.798
during the flood.

00:02:08.564 --> 00:02:11.806
My Subaru, it's a part of my tool-set

00:02:11.806 --> 00:02:14.606
that's just as important as my cameras.

00:02:14.606 --> 00:02:16.189
I wanted a car that I
could load my equipment in

00:02:16.189 --> 00:02:17.669
and travel around.

00:02:17.669 --> 00:02:21.877
As soon as I saw the five-door
Imprezas, I was like "yeah."

00:02:21.877 --> 00:02:24.739
I knew that this was gonna work.

00:02:24.739 --> 00:02:28.166
I appreciate the fact that
Subaru cares about the people

00:02:28.166 --> 00:02:31.368
that I care about, people like
the people in my community

00:02:31.368 --> 00:02:32.618
that they help.

00:02:33.524 --> 00:02:36.917
I'm doing a new film
about the flood recovery.

00:02:36.917 --> 00:02:39.869
Hopefully this documentary
will be my biggest contribution

00:02:39.869 --> 00:02:43.139
to the flood relief,
because as time progresses,

00:02:43.139 --> 00:02:46.888
people forget, and I want
to sort of remind everybody

00:02:46.888 --> 00:02:49.805
that this stuff is still happening.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.509
Hey, Ronnie!

00:02:53.509 --> 00:02:54.800
How are you doing?

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:58.189
- I'm behind ya, buddy, it gets tougher.

00:02:58.189 --> 00:03:00.200
- [Mark] Being back in West
Virginia has definitely

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.120
facilitated my passion
projects again, I'm actually

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.227
present in the state and
I can make work here,

00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:06.971
and I can talk about it.

00:03:06.971 --> 00:03:11.054
I'm not just dipping in
for a few days at a time.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.101
For me, it's not going out for a few hours

00:03:17.101 --> 00:03:21.149
and taking pictures, it's
days and maybe months.

00:03:21.149 --> 00:03:24.732
It's presence, it's
patience, it's honesty,

00:03:25.789 --> 00:03:28.381
it's a commitment, and
you're not just there

00:03:28.381 --> 00:03:32.548
to get a picture, you're
there to learn about somebody.

